# Settings for HAI's head on one machine. Copy to settings.env and edit.

# Where your Ollama server is, as seen from inside the container. On the same machine this is
# http://host.docker.internal:11434 (Docker Desktop knows the name; on Linux the compose file maps it to the machine);
# on another machine, its address. With no device roster the failover and heavy roles follow BRAIN_HOST, so one line
# covers all three.
BRAIN_HOST=http://host.docker.internal:11434
EMBED_HOSTS=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# Which models to use for each role. One model for all three is fine to start with.
BRAIN_MODEL=qwen3:8b
FAILOVER_MODEL=qwen3:8b
HEAVY_MODEL=qwen3:8b
EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text

# Context windows, in tokens. These fit any card; raise them once you have measured yours (docs/measure-your-own-box.md).
NUM_CTX=8192
BRAIN_NUM_CTX=8192
FAILOVER_NUM_CTX=8192
HEAVY_NUM_CTX=8192

# Start from the lab's measurements (docs/measure-your-own-box.md): place from the measured rows of the lab machine
# whose card resembles yours until your factory has measured your own. mothership = a 24 GB AMD card; bighonker and
# softserve = 8 GB NVIDIA cards. The compose file mounts the repository's menu/reference at /menu.
# HAI_POLICY_TABLE=/menu/policy.json
# PC1_REFERENCE_BOX=bighonker

# This machine. With no device roster it is PC1; settings that belong to one machine are named PC<n>_<SETTING>.
# PC1_NAME is what HAI calls it (shown to you); PC1_BRAIN_MODEL is the small model it falls back to on this machine.
PC1_NAME=My-PC
PC1_BRAIN_MODEL=qwen3:8b

# Who uses it. The first name is you; ADMIN_USERS may change settings. This is an example list: replace it.
PROFILES=Alex,Jamie
ADMIN_USERS=Alex
# The owner: the profile that approves changes and gets owner-only features. Prompts and messages name them.
OWNER_USER=Alex

# The Law persona, if you use it, focuses on one state: its name, and where its statutes and court opinions are read.
# LAW_STATE=Your State
# LAW_STATE_SOURCES=the state code at <site>; court opinions at <site>

# The factory on this machine reports to the head with a shared token (docs/quick-start.md, "Give the head its
# factory"). Put the token in a file under state/secrets/ and name it here; never the value itself.
P20_WORKER_TOKEN_FILE=/state/secrets/worker_token

# The lab's wall clock: notes, daily files and every human-facing time use this zone (an IANA name such as
# Europe/Berlin). UTC until you set yours.
TZ=UTC
